From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: TextBlock, brushes and font families

Text is most of what XAML pages show; there was no TextBlock. TextBlock lays its text out with DirectWrite (Text, FontSize, FontFamily, FontWeight, FontStyle, TextWrapping, TextAlignment, Padding, LineHeight, MaxLines, IsTextScaleFactorEnabled; BaselineOffset) and measures to it; XAML's own font (Segoe UI, XamlAutoFontFamily) is the desktop's message font unless that family is installed. Brush (composable) and SolidColorBrush (Color, Opacity), FontFamily (composable). The theme's colours come from the system colours of the desktop's look (Classic or Rounded, light or dark), not from Microsoft's XAML resources. Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0); the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
